sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    title HackMatch — US-001: Participant Registration and Email Verification — Email Verification Sequence
    actor Visitor
    participant UI as React Verification UI
    participant API as Express Auth API
    participant Firebase as Firebase Authentication
    participant DB as Supabase PostgreSQL

    Visitor->>UI: Open Firebase verification link
    UI->>Firebase: checkActionCode, then applyActionCode
    alt Link expired, invalid, consumed, or network fails
        Firebase--xUI: Explicit Firebase error
        UI-->>Visitor: Expired, invalid, or retry state
        opt Request replacement link
            Visitor->>UI: Submit registered email
            UI->>API: POST /api/auth/resend-verification
            alt Resend rate limited
                API-->>UI: 429 with retry guidance
            else Accepted, whether address is known or unknown
                API->>Firebase: Dispatch only for existing unverified account
                API-->>UI: Uniform 200 anti-enumeration response
            end
        end
    else Firebase email becomes verified
        UI->>API: POST /api/auth/verify-email with oobCode
        API->>Firebase: Attempt to consume the same action code
        alt Server obtains verified email
            Firebase-->>API: Verified email
            API->>DB: UPDATE participants SET is_verified=true
            API-->>UI: 200 verified, no session
        else Code was already consumed by the client
            Firebase--xAPI: INVALID_ACTION_CODE
            API-->>UI: 400 synchronization failure
            Note over UI,DB: Current risk: the UI ignores this response and omits the recovered email,<br/>so participants.is_verified may remain false.
        end
        UI-->>Visitor: Show success and require sign-in plus MFA
    end

    Visitor->>API: Attempt protected team action while DB unverified
    API->>DB: Read participant verification state
    DB-->>API: is_verified=false
    API-->>Visitor: 403 EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED, no data change
